+# Feature Specification: Fix SKU case, free-shipping threshold and line VAT rounding
+
+**Created**: 2026-11-17 | **Status**: Draft
+**Input**: Three reports: lower-case SKU refused (sales desk); €50.00 basket charged shipping (customer); line VAT one cent low (accounting).
+
+Affected README rules: Products (SKUs case-insensitive), Shipping (free from €50.00 after discounts), VAT (per line, half-up).
+
+## User Scenarios & Testing
+
+### User Story 1 - Lower-case SKU accepted (P1)
+Staff key in `lb-220` and the order is accepted as `LB-220`.
+**Acceptance**: Given product LB-220, when looked up as `lb-220` or ` lb-220 `, then it is found; an order with it is placed and shows `LB-220`.
+
+### User Story 2 - Free shipping at exactly €50.00 (P1)
+**Acceptance**: Goods after all discounts of exactly €50.00 ship free; €49.99 pays the weight band.
+
+### User Story 3 - VAT rounded half up per line (P1)
+**Acceptance**: A €1.99 line at 22% has VAT €0.44 (43.78c); exactly 0.5 cent (e.g. 25c at 10% = 2.5c) rounds up to 3c.
+
+## Requirements
+- **FR-001**: Catalogue lookup MUST treat SKUs case-insensitively and ignore surrounding spaces.
+- **FR-002**: Shipping MUST be free when goods after discounts, before VAT, are €50.00 or more.
+- **FR-003**: Line VAT MUST be rounded half up to the cent.
+
+## Success Criteria
+- SC-001: The three reported cases produce the expected results; all existing tests still pass.
+
+## Assumptions
+- Only the three reported defects are in scope; no rule changes, README unchanged.
